 Since the points $(-3,3)$, $(1,3)$, and $(0,0)$ lie on the parabola we can set up the following system of i equations in $a$, $b$, and $c$:
\begin{align*}
9a - 3b + c &= 3,\\
a + b + c &= 3,\\
c &= 0.
\end{align*}
To solve this linear system, we can substitute $c=0$ into the first two equations and solve
\begin{align*}
9a - 3b &= 3,\\
a + b &= 3,
\end{align*}
which results in $a=\frac{2}{3}$ and $b = \frac{7}{3}$. So, $100a + 10b + c = \frac{270}{3} = \boxed{90}$. <answer>
